{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1386339-can-you-make-the-whole-world-of-darkness-work-together-as-one-coherent-universe","id":1386339,"title":"Can you make the whole World of Darkness work together as one coherent universe?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-07T03:00:08-07:00","id":1386339,"title":"Can you make the whole World of Darkness work together as one coherent universe?","content":"Without a bunch of logical and thematic inconsistencies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T03:44:08-07:00","id":1386343,"title":"","content":"Short answer: no.<br /> <br /> Long answer: no, unless you're very generous with what counts as less than &quot;a bunch.&quot;<br /> <br /> For a pre-V5 game, the biggest problem on the logical side is the piecemeal fashion the history of the setting was written in. That is the general idea of &quot;how things are now,&quot; is actually not that hard to square, but when you add in the official stories of, &quot;how things got here,&quot; you can toss that out the window. The thematic side sorta depends on what you think a coherent universe needs out of each game line's thematic core. The biggest disconnect is the spectrum of how much hope there is in the themes of each line when you try to mesh them together. Vampires can worry about the themes of losing themselves to the Beast side by side changelings worrying about Banality gripping their fae souls, but vampires can only really aim to do as little damage as possible, while changelings can fight the coming Winter and rekindle human inspiration.<br /> <br /> V5 onwards adds a lot of unknowns obviously, but a clear wrinkle on the thematic end. The games that were either radically redone or added anew in the Revised era generally had major themes around the sudden changes brought on by the Revised metaplot. The Imbued hunters were suddenly let loose on the world. If they've been around for twenty years, a lot of their big themes around being a new phenomenon in the WoD go away. If you move the Reckoning up to 2020, then something immense has to happen to kick them off, which is going to mess with the themes of the other games (probably), or at least mess with things on the logical end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T04:21:33-07:00","id":1386346,"title":"","content":"Thanks \ud83d\ude0a. I appreciate the opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T05:04:30-07:00","id":1386357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1386339-can-you-make-the-whole-world-of-darkness-work-together-as-one-coherent-universe#post1386339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Without a bunch of logical and thematic inconsistencies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Short answer yes.<br /> <br /> More in depth answer is its complicated and can be difficult. It works best though with a coherent player character group, so like a Werewolfpack or Vampire Coterie, and you can have the whole World of Darkness setting in the background but your lens of storytelling is from the PC groups perspective. You can somewhat expand the PC group past one splat but you have to be careful. Like you shouldn't do a Fenrir/Bonegnawer/Fianna pack with a Nosferatu member, it doesn't mix well just like you couldn't really do a Ventrue, Gangrel, Tremere Coterie with a Child of Gaia tagging along. In those instances their respective societies would crap bricks if their situation is revealed. But if say they were Pariahs like a Ronin joining a group of Caitiffs it works much better.<br /> <br /> Wraiths being pretty much humans but dead and therefore apart of the supernatural world they could work well with most any groups, but they could have issues being incorporeal and alone on their side of the Shroud. But Mages, Changelings, and Mummies have relatively unrestrictive societies and they could get away with forming relations. And key connections like being Kinfolk or Kinain help, or just simply being neighbors growing up.<br /> <br /> See the background of virtually all the games revolve around mystery and uncertainty. Vampires don't have an explaination, the talk of God Cursing Caine has been mythologized by them they don't know what exactly happened, and several Noddists dispute whether Caine was Cursed by God himself, or the Angels who cursed him were cursing him with their own respective authority, and some even suspect Adam may actually have been responsible for the Curse banishing Caine to Nod, like some prehistoric Chorister.<br /> <br /> But the point is Vampire doesn't have proof of how the Universe works and they mostly concentrate on the temporal world. And Werewolf is a setting that pretty much just says their are three Universal Forces, There are also miscellaneous spirits and Gods, and Gaia could be above them all or below the Triat, it is all a mystery. They have a guess how vampires started, but they don't take it literally necessarily because they know it is just one story in the Silver Record and its super vague so maybe its an allegory. But their setting allows for mysteries beyond just you come from one of the Triat.<br /> <br /> Mage however is dominated by the idea that Humanities belief shapes the Universe. But this conflicts with the rest of the setting. Thing is not all mages believe or understand how belief interacts with causality and the whole of the Tapestry. But if you interpret Mage aligned with the Werewolf setting you can come to the conclusion that Humanity can shape the Tapestry but the Tapestry existed before humanity and it exists beyond humanity. So they are a major force for defining the Tellurian but they aren't the only force, Animals and Plants and stars have a sort of historical inertia and aren't completely under the sway of humanity.<br /> <br /> Changeling kind of believes everything supernatural came from the Fae, though maybe Ghosts and Mages represent more Humanity's personal magic. But they also understand that they can be wrong about history and their own history is held together by tales and myth. It really seems the Kiths weren't a thing in the Far Past and the Tuatha Fomorian divide may also be a mythologization of the more primordial Fae of Four Seasons approach.<br /> <br /> It could be the Universe exists. Animals came to be. Humanity learned to think. Fae came around, inspired humanity, stories of Gods and Demons arose around them. Spirits existed before the Gauntlet and they existed before humanity but Humanities Interaction with the Alien Fae seemed to have spawned a lot of how the spirit world formed. And Mages have some sort of spark that makes them push the boundaries of Humanities belief and worked to shape the world and be shaped by it.<br /> <br /> Hunters exist in a pure mystery. Deep dive and they may be the Agents of Angels, and those Angels may be separated by God, or they may be in touch with God, and God may have an aspect as the August Personage of Jade or he may be absent and was sundered into the Triat.<br /> <br /> Demon is both the most accommodating and the most narrow. They outright have a history with God and the Creation of the Universe that is pretty narrow, basically saying the Abrahamic faiths had an inkling of true history but they got a lot of the specifics wrong. But Demon also acknowledges that Creation exists on multiple planes of reality, like Adam and Eve were people, but were also tribes of early homo sapiens, and they were songs, and they were stories all on different planes of existence. Furthermore the books expand and reveal the Fallen weren't privy to all the Planes of existence, hence why they are ignorant of animism, and Devils also know that before being banished to the Abyss the Fallen host gave some of their memories to Lucifer, and they don't know what those memories were. And the Last House understood the secret that God hid the fate of Mortals souls from the Fallen, hence why they created the underworld out of fear of the Unknown.<br /> <br /> The big issue is Demon, unlike virtually all the other splats, made a decision to outright ignore the Umbra in their setting, so they only concentrate on the Material World and the Underworld. Other gamelines usually acknowledge aspects of the Tellurian that are a mystery to them, like Vampires can kind of conceive of the Umbra as a spirit world and the Underworld as a separate dimension, and Werewolves plumb the depths of the Universe but the Dreaming is kind of a mystery to them but they know it exists and can be explored. Demon just states Werewolves go into the Underworld when they step sideways to simplify the rules.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So basically TLDR you can have a coherent holistic World of Darkness if your PC groups is coherent and of one splat. That helps act as a lens to interpret the whole of Reality through. But if you have a mixed PC group things get trickier and trickier to juggle and some just snip and edit some parts of the setting to be more coherent, like Demon ignoring the Umbra, and Mage ignoring the Triat but Acknowledging the three fold aspect of Destruction/Stasis/Dynamism.<br /> <br /> Oh and technically if you do a Middle Kingdom game the whole setting there is unified and built to have all the Supernatural splats fit in each others paradigm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T06:12:12-07:00","id":1386375,"title":"","content":"My answer: Kinda Sorta. But you need to put a lot of work in and answer a bunch of setting questions for yourself.<br /> <br /> I ran a multisplat game, 6 players, each a different splat. Anansi, Western Wan Kuei, (Who i call Revenants), 2 Cainite Vampires, an Imbued Hunter and a Demon.<br /> <br /> I read thru the entire back catalogue of owod, filled about 2 notebooks with ideas and answers and then ran the campaign for 4 years. It went pretty well. But it's not Classic WoD. It's my iteration of the setting seen thru the lens of what i decided to keep and what i decided to jettison.<br /> <br /> I dont think the Revised or 20th settings could be amalgamated into a Unified WoD. The books were never written to agree with any of the other lines. But maybe WoD 5th could be made to work. I look forward to seeing if it's possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3399-hachiman","name":"hachiman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3399_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T08:25:16-07:00","id":1386409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1386339-can-you-make-the-whole-world-of-darkness-work-together-as-one-coherent-universe#post1386339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Without a bunch of logical and thematic inconsistencies.</div> </div> </div> </div>WoD doesn't work together as a coherent universe. But you *can* make it work (with fiat and headcanon).<br /> <br /> It's entirely doable to spin things in a way that make sense, as long as you're willing to favor some aspects of the Lore over others, and set for a general tone. It's easy enough to smother inconsistencies if you're willing to call &quot;unreliable narration&quot; everything and anyone that contradicts your PoV. Obviously, the elements you call false or uncertain are going to be the certainities and core elements of other people.<br /> <br /> WoD it's <b>contradictory</b>. There's no way arround this: If you want a unified setting, you will need to choose what aspects of the WoD you're going to emphasize and what aspects are going to get the short stick.<br /> <br /> But you can totally <i>believe </i>in a coherent WoD. Just be nice with the other Paradigms out there, and aknowledge that it's *your* take on WoD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T11:55:05-07:00","id":1386445,"title":"","content":"Thank you guys \ud83d\ude0a<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar754_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"754\" data-vbnamecard=\"754\">Eldagusto</a> is the Underworld the same as the Lower/Dark Umbra?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T12:40:23-07:00","id":1386456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1386339-can-you-make-the-whole-world-of-darkness-work-together-as-one-coherent-universe?p=1386445#post1386445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you guys \ud83d\ude0a<br /> <br /> <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> is the Underworld the same as the Lower/Dark Umbra?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah when I say Underworld I just mean all the ghosts stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T14:57:51-07:00","id":1386504,"title":"","content":"Those who know me can probably guess my answer and the writing that is to come.<br /> <br /> I say yes and my reason for this is summed up in perhaps my favorite string of four words in all metacosmic discussion within WoD: Multi-Resonance Layered Reality.<br /> <br /> This is a phrase coined by Demon the Fallen and one which serves the purpose of uniting the seemingly disparate gamelines into a rather cohesive picture that is paradoxically made all the more firm by its snags of contradiction. The idea is that, similar to the concept of Consensual Reality from Mage, reality in the World of Darkness is not any one concrete thing but instead a vast cosmos of potential which is realized in an infinite number of ways. This has to do both with the nature of The One, the dualistic conflict of Everything and Nothing, and the nature of humanity. I can go into more detail on my ideas on that if people like, but for now I'll move on to what Multi-Resonance Layered Reality was and is, particularly at its height to create an example.<br /> <br /> The Modern World of Darkness is a fallen world. The golden age is over, virtue is dying, the only hope for the world may be cleansing fire. That's the standard WoD as we know it in all its Gothic-Punk glory and it exists by having the potential of reality compressed by its now fallen state.<br /> <br /> To paraphrase metaphors from Demon the Fallen: Multi-Resonance Layered Reality is how it is simultaneously true that G-d created the world in seven days, creation arose from the cosmic sea of chaos, and that after the Big Bang it took ~13 billion years of cosmic development for our world to form as we know it. Each of these things, while contradictory, are the literal truth. This is because the world is unfettered energy and potential perceived via different wavelengths or resonances. So on certain resonance layers angels can dance on the heads of pins while on other resonance layers matter is slammed together in the quantum forge to create everything.<br /> <br /> In the beginning these things existed simultaneously and with infinite potential and while the fall caused reality to compress and slowly narrow into what we know it as today, the potential still remains, built into the cosmological fabric of time and space.<br /> <br /> Creation as defined by its being the balance point of Existence between Everything and Nothing has been evolving and adapting while trying to maintain its fragile homeostasis. The potential cataclysm of the Time of Judgement is the scales tipping, probably towards Nothing but potentially towards Everything. Either would be catastrophic to our understanding of life.<br /> <br /> So we live our lives and we struggle to make ourselves known and matter. To be a single point shining to prove its existence in the face of an uncaring world and by the twinkling of that light stretching the moment of Creation a little further for those to come after us.<br /> <br /> Everything and Nothing connected by the Multi-Resonance Layered Reality of Creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T17:50:56-07:00","id":1386569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1386339-can-you-make-the-whole-world-of-darkness-work-together-as-one-coherent-universe?p=1386357#post1386357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Oh and technically if you do a Middle Kingdom game the whole setting there is unified and built to have all the Supernatural splats fit in each others paradigm. </span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div>Middle Kingdom stuff is a big crossover,<br /> <br /> Hunter too<br /> <br /> I think it's a good idea, now I plan to write a sourcebook of HtR, which sets in the post-Judgement Day era, I refer to the two lines for more ideas","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T06:20:53-07:00","id":1386670,"title":"","content":"Maybe I'm dumb, or it comes from a setting I don't play, or I'm thinking of it as something else, but what is the Middle Kingdom?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T07:04:05-07:00","id":1386679,"title":"","content":"China \u2014 or, more generally, the Kindred of the East and the Year of the Lotus stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T07:04:36-07:00","id":1386680,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1386339-can-you-make-the-whole-world-of-darkness-work-together-as-one-coherent-universe?p=1386679#post1386679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">China \u2014 or, more generally, the Kindred of the East and the Year of the Lotus stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, Middle Kingdom refers to all Far East in supernatural view, which is a vague concept<br /> <br /> In reality it only refers to China</span></span></span></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 05-08-2020, 10:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T09:51:38-07:00","id":1386724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1386339-can-you-make-the-whole-world-of-darkness-work-together-as-one-coherent-universe#post1386339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Without a bunch of logical and thematic inconsistencies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, though it may not make sense to the characters in-universe it is possible to do via combining Mage\u2019s \u201cconsensus creates reality\u201d and Demon\u2019s \u201cmultiple layers of reality\u201d concept.<br /> <br /> The real trick is understanding that, at a metaphysical level, different splats are interacting with each other on different layers of reality.<br /> <br /> - Mages interact on a layer where Creation, Stasis, Dynamism and Entropy are metaphysical concepts and Adam/Eve/Caine are allogories of early human civilizations and their struggles. Vampires are thaumivores and werewolves are embodied spirits in this layer.<br /> <br /> - Werewolves interact on a layer where those are actual spiritual entities (Gaia, Weaver, Wyld and Wyrm respectively) and Caine was a mortal who was possessed by a powerful Bane (one probably associated with cannibalism). Mages are mortals who, knowingly or not, interact with all manner of spirits that warp reality and Vampires are wyrm-tainted infectious fomori in this layer.<br /> <br /> - Vampires are in a layer where all those cosmic forces were created by an omnipotent Creator and Caine was a real person cursed by Him. Mages aren\u2019t any one thing (they\u2019re people with true faith, hedge magic, psychic powers, advanced tech) and Lupines are some unknown entity (perhaps also cursed by God).<br /> <br /> - All three exist in a layer (\u201cthe game\u201d to be particularly meta about the layers of reality) where magick, gifts and disciplines all function and the individual metaphysics are probably irrelevant to the situation at hand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T14:49:14-07:00","id":1386783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1386339-can-you-make-the-whole-world-of-darkness-work-together-as-one-coherent-universe#post1386339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Without a bunch of logical and thematic inconsistencies.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No because a fully realized Universe is filled with thematic and logical inconsistancies. The Real world is messy. Its filled with contradictions in physics, people arguing about history and so on.. a world that includes everything that exists PLUS adds stuff should be confusing and inconsistant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T15:33:48-07:00","id":1386797,"title":"","content":"@Lian very good point!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T15:35:08-07:00","id":1386798,"title":"","content":"Yes, you can. Although I do think it requires a good ST who is willing to put into the work needed to create a comprehensive setting.<br /> <br /> The original five game lines are largely compatible. They were meant to be. There was even meant to be crossover in terms of PCs. Mechanically that was never really the case since there were too many game line specific mechanics for many powers. Those always had to have fudges. But in terms of the setting itself, it's fairly consistent. There are some seeming inconsistencies, but they can be easily resolved by a single Storyteller. The only reason it broke down in the Revised era is that the various game line developers established their feudal fiefs and couldn't work together. But a single ST doesn't have that problem. They just need to decide what they want to take precedent. And most of those issues are high metaphysical stuff that won't come into play for 99% of games. The other issues can be resolved simply by damping down on the actual # of supernatural creatures out there.<br /> <br /> I only utilize the first game lines as that was comprehensive outside of small 1 book WoD books like the original Mummy or Sorcerer. I considered the additional game lines (the new Mummy, Hunter, KotE, Demon) etc. to be desperate attempts at cash grabs and not part of the original vision. But since even those were built on the earlier foundations, I suspect they too could be made to work.<br /> <br /> I think the real issue is how an ST should present the setting so that all elements are (theoretically) present, but for the most point don't interrupt what players expect from the game their playing. In other words, Vampire players want a game where they mainly interact with mortals and other Vampires. They don't want to be interrupted and dealing with werewolves or strange umbra creatures... <i>most of the time</i>. Those same players may still have lots of fun with a specific plot involving werewolves or ghosts or whatever as long as it doesn't seem to hijack the game, and they still want to see the setting mainly through the eyes of vampire genre expectations. They typically don't want a Monster Mash that detracts from vampire specific themes. They want their vampire game to FEEL like a vampire game even if somewhere in the background are lupines, mages, ghosts, and fae.<br /> <br /> How an ST blends everything in will be specific to them and their playing group. I'm fairly confidant that I run a single coherent World of Darkness universe in my chronicles, and can probably answer 99%+ of the questions asked of me OOC either immediately or with a little thought. It just will likely be different than someone else's conception who emphasize or prioritize certain things.<br /> <br /> One hang up is that certain players insist that their favored splat is correct because they actually know how X works. But in fact, other splats also know that they are correct as well. Very often, if you actually pay attention to the books, each splat only knows so much through direct evidence and they simply ASSUME a lot of things. But if you change those assumptions, it won't contradict their direct evidence.<br /> <br /> What is mainly needed is a skilled ST that can introduce other elements into the game without disrupting the genre expectations players of that game want to experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T07:53:12-07:00","id":1386973,"title":"","content":"While I already outlined my \u201cmany layers\u201d answer, one thing I think is worth asking too is \u201cHow often do you have players using more two of the supernatural types in the same campaign?\u201d<br /> <br /> I ask because the fewer \u201clayers\u201d you have to have interact for your campaign, the easier a consistent world becomes. Merging just Vampire and Wraith practically writes itself. Merging Changeling and Mage is similarly easy. Vampire and Mage can also work reasonably well. HtR and Mage can also be pretty interesting if you let the Imbued recognize \u201cpurple auras\u201d are another type of mortal who help them.<br /> <br /> Basically, nearly any two splats* can be merged relatively easily (minor splats like old-style mummies and mortal hunters almost don\u2019t count in this regard), its when you start adding a third or fourth splat that problems can start to occur.<br /> <br /> And in my experience, unless you have an exceptionally large group (6+ players) and explicitly open it up to multiple splats, you\u2019re probably not going to see more than two splats mixing. The biggest campaign I ever ran was 14 players (it worked largely by using an entire college classroom to play and treating it as a mini-LARP where I only stepped in to RP a particular NPC or resolve something mechanically) and we had 12 mages, a vampire and an old-style mummy for PCs.<br /> <br /> Everything else was typically a case of a lone player and \u201cI wanna play with the group, but just can\u2019t wrap my head around playing X... can I play Y instead?\u201d and even then it was more typical to go splat adjacent (ex. playing a Dhampir or old-school Mummy in a vampire game) than completely cross-splat.<br /> <br /> The biggest outlier I\u2019ve found in \u201cdoes not play well with others; mechanically, socially or metaphysically\u201d are the werewolves. Their Crinos forms just break the mechanics of everything else with ridiculous dice pools and how their rage interacts with willpower and social mechanics can make them practically unplayable outside of combat in a mixed chronicle unless the player is willing to build a \u201cnon-combat\u201d garou (in quotes because even a 2/2/2 in physicals becomes a 6/3/5 that soaks agg, regenerates lethal and deals 7 dice of lethal damage in melee just by entering Crinos).<br /> <br /> Similarly, their cosmology is the most dogmatic. You can explore the main themes of Vampire without ever involving an Antediluvian or even a Methuselah or mentioning Caine being cursed by God as literal truth. You can explore the main themes of Mage without making any assumptions about the cosmological basis for vampires and werewolves existing or why they can\u2019t be allies.<br /> <br /> Werewolf though is centered around an apocalyptic conflict in a very specific cosmology that labels just about everything that\u2019s not another Garou as some perversion of nature that must be destroyed to appease their insatiable rage. Mages are, at best, thieves of spiritual essence that \u201crightfully\u201d belongs to the Garou to puppets of the Weaver and/or Wyrm at worst. Vampires are Wyrm-tainted abominations. Wraiths and Mummies are loaded down with entropic Wyrm-taint due to their ties to the Dark Umbra.<br /> <br /> This is why the Lupines in my Vampire campaign aren\u2019t Garou, but mortals under a separate divine curse (for their progenitor\u2019s hubris and cannibalism) who have similarly twisted divine power into disciplines and that is passed on by an infectious bite. It both fits better thematically (since everyone\u2019s playing either a vampire and it\u2019s all about dealing with a curse you didn\u2019t ask for) and mechanically.<br /> <br /> No one is playing one now, but depending on where things are at in the sandbox when a PC death occurs, a player could choose one of these Lupines and not be unbalanced with the remaining vampire PCs because they\u2019re built using disciplines, they must kill/feed to power them and struggle with their humanity and, while they can be active in daylight (a compensation for no ghouling or blood bonds) their disciplines and other supernatural abilities only function at night (i.e. they\u2019re a mere mortals during the times a vampire can\u2019t be active and would have to act through ghouls).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T10:02:47-07:00","id":1387003,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1328\" data-vbnamecard=\"1328\">Chris24601</a> you make some really good points. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T17:53:46-07:00","id":1387134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1386339-can-you-make-the-whole-world-of-darkness-work-together-as-one-coherent-universe?p=1386973#post1386973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I already outlined my \u201cmany layers\u201d answer, one thing I think is worth asking too is \u201cHow often do you have players using more two of the supernatural types in the same campaign?\u201d<br /> <br /> I ask because the fewer \u201clayers\u201d you have to have interact for your campaign, the easier a consistent world becomes. Merging just Vampire and Wraith practically writes itself. Merging Changeling and Mage is similarly easy. Vampire and Mage can also work reasonably well. HtR and Mage can also be pretty interesting if you let the Imbued recognize \u201cpurple auras\u201d are another type of mortal who help them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Merging Mage stops being easy if you start asking questions about things... which is inevitably going to come up via mages speculating on the nature of their allies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Basically, nearly any two splats* can be merged relatively easily (minor splats like old-style mummies and mortal hunters almost don\u2019t count in this regard), its when you start adding a third or fourth splat that problems can start to occur.<br /> <br /> And in my experience, unless you have an exceptionally large group (6+ players) and explicitly open it up to multiple splats, you\u2019re probably not going to see more than two splats mixing. The biggest campaign I ever ran was 14 players (it worked largely by using an entire college classroom to play and treating it as a mini-LARP where I only stepped in to RP a particular NPC or resolve something mechanically) and we had 12 mages, a vampire and an old-style mummy for PCs.<br /> <br /> Everything else was typically a case of a lone player and \u201cI wanna play with the group, but just can\u2019t wrap my head around playing X... can I play Y instead?\u201d and even then it was more typical to go splat adjacent (ex. playing a Dhampir or old-school Mummy in a vampire game) than completely cross-splat.<br /> <br /> The biggest outlier I\u2019ve found in \u201cdoes not play well with others; mechanically, socially or metaphysically\u201d are the werewolves. Their Crinos forms just break the mechanics of everything else with ridiculous dice pools and how their rage interacts with willpower and social mechanics can make them practically unplayable outside of combat in a mixed chronicle unless the player is willing to build a \u201cnon-combat\u201d garou (in quotes because even a 2/2/2 in physicals becomes a 6/3/5 that soaks agg, regenerates lethal and deals 7 dice of lethal damage in melee just by entering Crinos).<br /> <br /> Similarly, their cosmology is the most dogmatic. You can explore the main themes of Vampire without ever involving an Antediluvian or even a Methuselah or mentioning Caine being cursed by God as literal truth. You can explore the main themes of Mage without making any assumptions about the cosmological basis for vampires and werewolves existing or why they can\u2019t be allies.<br /> <br /> Werewolf though is centered around an apocalyptic conflict in a very specific cosmology that labels just about everything that\u2019s not another Garou as some perversion of nature that must be destroyed to appease their insatiable rage. Mages are, at best, thieves of spiritual essence that \u201crightfully\u201d belongs to the Garou to puppets of the Weaver and/or Wyrm at worst. Vampires are Wyrm-tainted abominations. Wraiths and Mummies are loaded down with entropic Wyrm-taint due to their ties to the Dark Umbra. </div> </div> </div>Mummies don't ping on Sense Wyrm unless they're bane mummies, mages often get a pass because they slip through the cracks and/or might have common ground depending on paradigm (never if they try to suck caerns with Prime, but that tenet is ironclad), and changelings can more often than not be approached as friends. Meanwhile, Vampire and Demon try to turn the entire setup into Literally Read Christian Horror, and Mage tries to filter everything through post-modern hermeticism, even when pieces of itself don't fit that operating view and would be better off literally communicating with their ancestors or what have you instead of Hermetic circumlocutions and speculation about whether they're really the ancestors, beings that assume their forms, or fragments of memory that linger in the cosmos. I'd worry less about what Werewolf says in a crossover and more about whether or not Vampire is going to try to make everything about Noddism, because even Vampire hasn't necessarily tried to impose that on itself at every turn, and it doesn't need to be the absolute origin of whatever curse vampires suffer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is why the Lupines in my Vampire campaign aren\u2019t Garou, but mortals under a separate divine curse (for their progenitor\u2019s hubris and cannibalism) who have similarly twisted divine power into disciplines and that is passed on by an infectious bite. It both fits better thematically (since everyone\u2019s playing either a vampire and it\u2019s all about dealing with a curse you didn\u2019t ask for) and mechanically. </div> </div> </div>Lupines have never been presented as making more lupines with an infectious bite. They're what Vampire views Garou as, with W:tA easily slotted in if you want to play crossover.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No one is playing one now, but depending on where things are at in the sandbox when a PC death occurs, a player could choose one of these Lupines and not be unbalanced with the remaining vampire PCs because they\u2019re built using disciplines, they must kill/feed to power them and struggle with their humanity and, while they can be active in daylight (a compensation for no ghouling or blood bonds) their disciplines and other supernatural abilities only function at night (i.e. they\u2019re a mere mortals during the times a vampire can\u2019t be active and would have to act through ghouls). </div> </div> </div>Even if they're built using Disciplines, that's kind of like saying that you won't unbalance a game by letting someone play in a V:tM game with the powers of a Demon of Iron and Violence from KotE. That's a lot of dots beyond most other characters, and if they can move around during the day, they have a huge strategic advantage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T08:09:49-07:00","id":1387274,"title":"","content":"Saur Ops, we\u2019ve debated the Mage/Werewolf thing before and from those debates it\u2019s clear we have such different views of both lines that rehashing all that is fairly pointless.<br /> <br /> The new things relevant to THIS discussion though are;<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1386339-can-you-make-the-whole-world-of-darkness-work-together-as-one-coherent-universe?p=1387134#post1387134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lupines have never been presented as making more lupines with an infectious bite. They're what Vampire views Garou as, with W:tA easily slotted in if you want to play crossover.</div> </div> </div> </div>My Vampire campaign, my rules.<br /> <br /> Garou don\u2019t exist in my Vampire campaign.<br /> <br /> The Lupines in my campaign are descended from a divine curse (traditionally associated with Lycaon for his cannibalism, filicide and hubris). They have an infectious bite because the themes of the campaign are how you deal with an affliction you never asked for but now suffer from.<br /> <br /> My Lupines reinforce the theme of the supernatural as monstrous and the struggle to maintain one\u2019s humanity in the face of needing to kill to survive.<br /> <br /> There is no Gaia, nor Weaver, Wyld nor Wyrm in my Vampire campaign. There is the Triune God, True Faith, ghosts, biblical demons and the monsters born from twisting the curses laid down by divine (or infernal) powers. That fits a lot better with my Gothic horror themes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even if they're built using Disciplines, that's kind of like saying that you won't unbalance a game by letting someone play in a V:tM game with the powers of a Demon of Iron and Violence from KotE. That's a lot of dots beyond most other characters, and if they can move around during the day, they have a huge strategic advantage. </div> </div> </div>You misunderstand... Lupines aren\u2019t built like WtA with disciplines on top.<br /> <br /> They\u2019re built like vampires.<br /> <br /> There is no rage or gnosis or stepping sideways, nor being able to change into any of five forms.<br /> <br /> They have the standard vampire special abilities modified by their \u201cclan weakness\u201d and 3 dots of disciplines, one of which must be in their custom discipline; Lycanthropy;<br /> <br /> <b>Lycanthropy</b><br /> 1) Wolf Form: as Protean 3, but wolf only.<br /> 2) Heightened Senses: as Auspex 1.<br /> 3) Feral Claws: as Protean 2.<br /> 4) Wolf Hide: mechanically as Serpentis 3, but no willpower cost and can\u2019t squeeze (appearance-wise it\u2019s your classic horror film wolf-man).<br /> 5) Hybrid Form: mechanically as Vicissitude 4 (appearance-wise it\u2019s a hybrid form akin to Crinos).<br /> <br /> Their other \u201cclan\u201d disciplines are Celerity and Potence. They can also learn Animalism, Fortitude and Presence (though instead of being paralyzed and unable to act out of fascination, it\u2019s due to supernatural terror), but not other disciplines. They power their disciplines (including attribute boosting and healing) by feeding on the flesh of mortals (gain \u201cblood\u201d points equal to half the health levels dealt by their bite attacks).<br /> <br /> Their \u201cClan\u201d weakness is that they cannot blood bond or ghoul, nor can they spend \u201cblood\u201d or use their disciplines during daylight hours. They also take aggravated damage from silver, but do not take damage from sunlight.<br /> <br /> So yes, they can move around during the day, but they\u2019re no stronger than a mortal and actually weaker than a typical ghoul that vampires will use to protect themselves and carry about their daytime affairs (for example, a ghoul can use its disciplines during daylight hours... the werewolf cannot).<br /> <br /> In other words, my Lupines are on par with a vampire of similar experience and generation and are man-eating monsters, not noble warriors for Gaia (who, again, doesn\u2019t exist in this campaign... or if she does, is another biblical demon masquerading as a pagan god).<br /> <br /> You don\u2019t have to like it, but my players do and that\u2019s all that matters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1328,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","user":"Chris24601","date":". 05-10-2020, 11:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T11:25:45-07:00","id":1387301,"title":"","content":"You can, but you'd have to remove the blatant inconsistencies. Retcon D:TF and make the whole Caine spiel a myth popularized by Vampires due Christianity have a steep prevalence with Rome adopting it later one (Rome may I remind being the utmost headquarters of the western Kindred. Besides that most of the splats DO work very well together if you read through all their major books like I have. Actually the biggest misconception about the oWoD fanbase is taking it as if the splats aren't already in the same universe- they clearly are at this point considering the precedents established. (looking at you Xerxe Jones and your &quot;Spirit Nuke&quot; that totally wasn't a plot convenience to flat out not write Wraith anymore.. besides this there are many more pieces that can be referenced clearly showing all the splats DO reside in the same universe).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T11:26:45-07:00","id":1387302,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1328\" data-vbnamecard=\"1328\">Chris24601</a> you\u2019ve totally changed the setting, but that\u2019s cool. Everyone\u2019s campaign is different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T13:21:55-07:00","id":1387318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1386339-can-you-make-the-whole-world-of-darkness-work-together-as-one-coherent-universe?p=1387302#post1387302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> you\u2019ve totally changed the setting, but that\u2019s cool. Everyone\u2019s campaign is different.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did I \u201ctotally\u201d change the setting though?<br /> <br /> The Vampire part is entirely intact and it\u2019s lore only details Lupines to the extent that they\u2019re dangerous things in the wilds that can eat vampires.<br /> <br /> All I did was exclude the other worlds\u2019 truths from Vampire.<br /> <br /> One of the things Mage got into, particularly in the final chapters of Ascension, but I believe also in the Revised Storyteller\u2019s Guide, was the idea that it\u2019s actually \u201cWorldS of Darkness\u201d where each game line (each table when you get down to it) occupies it\u2019s own parallel world where the aspects of the others were reflected dimly or even not at all.<br /> <br /> Mine is just one of those where \u201cnot at all\u201d reigns because we\u2019re after a \u2018back to basics\u2019 game.<br /> <br /> The discussion from the Mage book though did further suggest that pathways between these Worlds existed that could allow those from one world to enter another... essentially canonizing the concept of the Crossover with an \u201cofficial\u201d explanation of how all the disparate elements fit together.<br /> <br /> This is, in part, where my idea of each splat being its own \u201clayer\u201d of reality (as expressed in Demon regarding the Creation myth) came from.<br /> <br /> But \u201cInfinite Worlds of Darkness\u201d works too. Each Storyteller\u2019s decisions of how things fit together for their campaign is one of those infinite worlds and so every interpretation is right in at least one of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T13:44:40-07:00","id":1387320,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1328\" data-vbnamecard=\"1328\">Chris24601</a> You did change werewolves from noble warriors of Gaia to demonic creatures who spread their curse by infection. I get that you\u2019re trying to go back to basics, but that\u2019s REALLY basic. Werewolves haven\u2019t been \u201cLupines\u201d since literally a year after the first game was published (I know this for sure cause I used to talk to a guy online who actually played with Mark Rein-Hagen in one of the original Vampire playtest groups).<br /> <br /> That being said, I personally like the idea of the World of Darkness being one coherent setting that includes all the splats, but a lot of people seem to disagree. I think your version is really cool and it would make a great alternate universe. But as long as your players like it, that\u2019s really all that matters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T19:04:27-07:00","id":1387390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1386339-can-you-make-the-whole-world-of-darkness-work-together-as-one-coherent-universe?p=1387274#post1387274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Saur Ops, we\u2019ve debated the Mage/Werewolf thing before and from those debates it\u2019s clear we have such different views of both lines that rehashing all that is fairly pointless.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bringing up that Garou don't immediately blenderize all other game protagonists out of hand isn't a different point of view; it's in the presentation of crossover in each and every splatbook.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> My Vampire campaign, my rules. </div> </div> </div>I was talking about the presentation in the books. If Lupines could infect others with an attack, that would lead to a very different presentation in the antagonists section of all the non-W:tA games. Instead, they're presented as not reproducing particularly quickly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You misunderstand... Lupines aren\u2019t built like WtA with disciplines on top.<br /> <br /> They\u2019re built like vampires. </div> </div> </div>No, that was fairly straightforward and obvious. That's why I mentioned Demons of Iron and Violence, which are also built with Disciplines alone (aside from a pile of extra health levels, anyway), though I was perplexed about whether or not you were using the quantity of dots in the Lupine entry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T12:12:42-07:00","id":1389403,"title":"","content":"The 'canonical' response would probably be 'not really, unless you really wanted.' Back in the day the systems were meant to be more or less self-contained with some overlap, and it was a known problem that they wouldn't fit together neatly,<br /> <br /> I think it's more of a qualified yes. It's qualified because what defines 'coherent' and 'consistent' is going to depend on one's personal suspension of disbelief and how you regard the material and how willing you are to work with it. For most people its probably not worth the time or effort to try to come up with explanations for every little inconsistency or variation, and you're never likely to get a nice, neat, non-kludgy answer that will satisfy everyone (Suspension of Disbelief at work.)<br /> <br /> As long as you don't care that it may cause others to disagree, I think you can find your own personal answer (and even find agreement with others) to bridge all the various systems together. Its simply a matter of persistence and how willing to have your preconceptions broken you are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25533,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","user":"Mister_Dunpeal","date":". 05-17-2020, 03:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T13:57:09-07:00","id":1389447,"title":"","content":"I am also a fan of a comprehensive World of Darkness, with Cainites and Garou and Awakened, etc. In trying to assemble a cosmology that is at least roughly unified, I've found the best approach to be a willingness to trash some of the assumptions of each gameline without ripping them up entirely.<br /> <br /> For Vampire and Demon, the Abrahamic God does exist, but is not quite equivalent with The One, instead being one of the largest identifiable aspects. The Demons are remembering a lot of particulars wrong, though a lot of it is at least vaguely accurate.<br /> <br /> For Werewolf, the Garou are essentially correct in their belief that Gaia and the (conflicts of) the Triat are one of the most important features of reality, in that they are another crucial aspect of The One. But again, not everything; there is more between the Gaia Realm and the Umbra than is dreamt of in their philosophy.<br /> <br /> Mages are correct to a degree about Consensus Reality, in that they theoretically have the potential to rewrite Reality in almost any way they like. But in practice, Reality has its own existing opinions on the matter (e.g. the Triat), and is generally capable of putting arrogant Mages in their place.<br /> <br /> What is The One? My current theory is essentially pantheistic: The One is The Tellurian, the multiverse of interconnected realms that make up the World of Darkness, bounded by the primal chaos of the Deep Umbra and the absolute nothingness of the Abyss. If you make the analogy of The One being a single human being, every Bad Thing in the World of Darkness boils down to an Internal problem, the equivalent of a physical or psychological dysfunction that needs to heal or work itself out, or an External problem, some kind of Eldritch Horror capable of 'attacking' something on that scale. Generally speaking, God and Gaia don't 'concern themselves' with the plights of individuals because, by analogy, the concerns of individuals are the concerns of cells or atoms; they care about the fate of limbs and organs, not the condition of individual cells. Mages Ascending, meanwhile, is the equivalent of a reproductive process, the splitting off of a portion that has grown to the point of becoming its own Reality (or Eldritch Horror....).<br /> <br /> There are obviously a lot of details that get trampled in such an interpretation, particularly the teleological aspects of most gamelines, but that's intentional. In a lot of ways, it's about accommodating the mechanical realities of the games while being willing to play fast and loose with the more open and intentionally-mysterious aspects of the lore. There's a lot of particular details I haven't quite decided even with the framework has been figured out; I dunno whether I want to make Oblivion an Internal or External problem, for example.<br /> <br /> While I enjoy the exercise, and like the answer I've come up with, I do think that Heavy Arms' initial response was probably the best: depends on how much thematic inconsistency you define as &quot;a bunch,&quot; but mostly no, lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T18:05:07-07:00","id":1389504,"title":"","content":"Thanks \ud83d\ude0a...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T06:01:05-07:00","id":1389943,"title":"","content":"I have discussed it before and yes it is kinda possible with main Focus on Mage and how believ changes the history. First there where humans. Where they come from and if they where created by God is not really to figure out but let just start with there whas existence in the beginning. As I said before many humans changed on how they thought they universe whas, like originally people think the live on flat plate and the stars are just holes in the atmospheric barrier that protect them from the world fire. Then humans started to believe the world is a ball which where enough to make it able to &quot;prove&quot; that is really round. And with the order of reason wanting to take away humanity from religious belief they either intentiones or without knowing invented alternative history where humanity where not like originally created from God with Adam and Eve and the world is young but instead really old and we just are just a minute on the cosmic year. So all those mythical beasts where interepreted as dinousaurs etc and with the believ the world changed after the people. So are the logical flaws explainable because a those still came from a history that whas now rewritten and while it whas true before it is now needed to retcon and b with mouth to mouth transition things just get lost or turn out wrong and this historic believ is just not as strong as the written &quot;fact&quot; that all the people believ in from","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T16:34:31-07:00","id":1390407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1386339-can-you-make-the-whole-world-of-darkness-work-together-as-one-coherent-universe?p=1389943#post1389943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have discussed it before and yes it is kinda possible with main Focus on Mage and how believ changes the history. First there where humans. Where they come from and if they where created by God is not really to figure out but let just start with there whas existence in the beginning. As I said before many humans changed on how they thought they universe whas, like originally people think the live on flat plate and the stars are just holes in the atmospheric barrier that protect them from the world fire. Then humans started to believe the world is a ball which where enough to make it able to &quot;prove&quot; that is really round. And with the order of reason wanting to take away humanity from religious belief they either intentiones or without knowing invented alternative history where humanity where not like originally created from God with Adam and Eve and the world is young but instead really old and we just are just a minute on the cosmic year. So all those mythical beasts where interepreted as dinousaurs etc and with the believ the world changed after the people. So are the logical flaws explainable because a those still came from a history that whas now rewritten and while it whas true before it is now needed to retcon and b with mouth to mouth transition things just get lost or turn out wrong and this historic believ is just not as strong as the written &quot;fact&quot; that all the people believ in from</div> </div> </div> </div>Focusing on Mage just gives you a Mage setting, not a theoretical Grand Unified WoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T00:38:44-07:00","id":1390503,"title":"","content":"Yeah they all work together quite easily. <br /> A thing you gotta remember<br /> <br /> Vampires are lying about lies. (They're also far more disconnected to magic than the rest) <br /> Changers are honour bound &quot;historical revisionists&quot; <br /> Mages are conceited to delusion. <br /> Fae are fundamentally adverse to telling a straight story.<br /> Ghosts have nothing.<br /> Demons are victims of the demiurge and'll remember what the demiurge wants them to remember. <br /> <br /> <br /> So, if you take some things with a grain of salt, take some things as metaphor and some metaphors as literal, it all works. Reading up on Gnosticism/Hermeticism helps (ancient belief systems that encompass other belief systems; you'll also understand Tremere/Settites/Mages a lot better)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T02:29:49-07:00","id":1390515,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a> interesting. Thanks.<br /> <br /> Do you think the Demiurge in WoD is male or do you think it has no gender?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T05:52:50-07:00","id":1390538,"title":"","content":"I think it <i>Identifies</i> as male, because he's a dick that's top dog and masculinity was all the authoritarian rage back then. Nowadays... maybe he'd take the form of a middle class white woman, since they're the peak force in society now, amrite? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br /> The demiurge is an immortal divine being beyond the shell of anatomy. In all seriousness I feel the demiurge wants to keep hidden. The Masquerade is a metaphore for how today's rulers want to hide from the spotlight. I think that applies to gods too. The main thing about seperating the demiurge from &quot;the one above all&quot; is that the demiurge is a villain who needs to be toppled by the collective consciousnesses of humanity, which I think is basically the goal of <i>Mage </i>with the whole ascension thing. The Demiurge wants to be a myth; maybe he had all the power back in the time of Adam and Eve or the Tower of Babel, but now an appearance would be counter to keeping the material world as it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T08:11:51-07:00","id":1390554,"title":"","content":"I am a white girl \ud83d\ude0a<br /> <br /> But for real, I like your conception of the Demiurge. I guess mages searching for Ascension would by definition be struggling against him/them/it. I don\u2019t know if I would ever do a Gnostic cosmology, but that definitely has potential.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T11:49:33-07:00","id":1390595,"title":"","content":"Cosmology doesn't matter that much to a lot of games in practice. Werewolf may be an exception because you interact with spirits so much. So it's entirely possible to have a game where the truth behind the various myths is unknown and the focus is on the character's actions and the things they interact with. The games are out of balance and there are a few crossover rule concerns, but honestly those can be overcome with a few rule tweaks.<br /> <br /> The bigger issues for me are themes of the respective games and supernatural glut, especially politically.<br /> <br /> Let's say we have a corrupt mayer in some city your party is in. Maybe he's controlled by the Ventrue or maybe the Giovanni, maybe he is in league with Pentex, maybe he has a literal deal with the Devil or demons, maybe he is controlled by the Syndicate or Nephandi, maybe he is controlled by one of the numerous other factions across numerous game lines that have influence in politics, wealth, or mind control. There are so many groups out there secretly controlling the world that it gets silly, plus what ever normal humans are doing too. What about the deep dark woods where people tell scary stories about - do the Garou live there, are their nature spirits, is it haunted by wraiths, is there a Gangrel in there, are the Unseelie faeries, is it corrupted by the Wyrm, is it just normal? Of course you can choose one of these options for the above questions, but when you have so many options and so many creatures that magic looses a bit of its magic. <br /> <br /> When it comes to actually playing games with all these creatures thrown in, then I feel like the themes of one or more games will often suffer. This may be the most important hurdle for me personally. If you have a game with a mage, a vampire, and a werewolf maybe you can ignore the conflicting cosmologies and be alright and maybe you can tweak the rules a bit and balance out the creatures, those won't be problems. What will be a problem is what this group actually does. Are they going to do battle with banes to protect the forest, will they fight against becoming less human, will they get involved in political schemes adjacent the Prince, will the try to escape from the oppressive Technocracy agents in the area? They could do any of those things, but basically we have to go with the themes of one game line to the detriment of the others. About the only sort of crossover that is consistent with all game lines is that there is some super evil enemy and various creatures need to work together to fight it, which still fails to utilize much of the valuable options in the various games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T14:03:02-07:00","id":1390619,"title":"","content":"I think it all fits together about as well as the real world all fits together, which is <i>not </i>to say that the myths of every human culture all fit neatly together. The real problem arises when you try to take all the mythologies and cosmologies as literal truth that must be reconciled into a unified field theory of Darkness. That can\u2019t be done. They\u2019re all very deliberately designed to work for their particular adherents and not really for any one else. All those things are just narrative models for understanding the world with a limited perspective and a particular set of experiences. It\u2019s the fans that tend to turn them into objective truths and complain that the setting doesn\u2019t make any sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T15:59:36-07:00","id":1390645,"title":"","content":"@BlackFlag that makes a lot of sense","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T18:57:21-07:00","id":1390679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1386339-can-you-make-the-whole-world-of-darkness-work-together-as-one-coherent-universe?p=1390503#post1390503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah they all work together quite easily.<br /> A thing you gotta remember<br /> <br /> Vampires are lying about lies. (They're also far more disconnected to magic than the rest)<br /> Changers are honour bound &quot;historical revisionists&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>They aren't really revising anything unless they're Mnetic Mokole. They are engaging in some serious values dissonance, especially where it comes to Garou saying &quot;Yeah, we kicked your asses and won the fight. What of it?&quot; to the Fera, because to do otherwise would deny their ancestors the Glory of those battles, which would be compromising the Honor of modern Garou for showing such an affront.<br /> <br /> As is often pointed out, however, Galliards (as well as Ragabashes and Theurges) don't rely very much on Honor, but Wisdom, which is much more interested in retrieving objective takes on situations. Note that Corax are also big into this, Bastet like to keep secrets (so you can get something more objective out of them, for a price), and Mokole are charged with keeping as objective a record as possible of all changer history and also recovering lost truths lurking in their collective Mnesis. Rokea are also presented as being honest and forthright to an almost pathological degree (Valor, bolstered by Harmony and Innovation), but they have far less contact with everyone else, because they're trying to stay in their own collective lane.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mages are conceited to delusion.<br /> Fae are fundamentally adverse to telling a straight story. </div> </div> </div>That really varies by kith. Boggans and trolls tend to be to the point, for instance. Not everyone is a pooka.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ghosts have nothing. </div> </div> </div>They have the collective scraps of human history to hang onto and fight over, moliated tooth and nail. While the focus is typically on what an individual does when faced with Fetters, Passions, and a Shadow, they do dwell on the past to the point of obsession, so their thoughts with regards to those things are likely cogent and accurate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Demons are victims of the demiurge and'll remember what the demiurge wants them to remember.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, if you take some things with a grain of salt, take some things as metaphor and some metaphors as literal, it all works. Reading up on Gnosticism/Hermeticism helps (ancient belief systems that encompass other belief systems; you'll also understand Tremere/Settites/Mages a lot better) </div> </div> </div>Hermeticism only really applies in Mage, since that's what the Purple Paradigm is built on. Other games flip it one or more birds (W:tA probably flips it the most, courtesy of multi-armed Mokole holding Corax on each middle finger, who themselves are also flipping both partially-transformed middle fingers).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T19:26:15-07:00","id":1390683,"title":"","content":"Another thing about Hermetism is that it relies on some nebulous &quot;One&quot;, some monotheistic-unitary force that basically has illusions to the Abrahamic god (which Hermetism seemingly got alot of inspiration from). Thats all fine and dandy, but how does this hold with the existence of the Triat in oWoD? With that standard brought up I don't know how Hermeticism could unify the cosmologies of oWoD since that conflicts right off the bat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T20:24:43-07:00","id":1390692,"title":"","content":"I thought Mage was originally based on chaos magick. But yeah, the problem with totalizing theories of the universe like Hermeticism is that while you can cram everything into them, the things you\u2019ve crammed in probably don\u2019t resemble their original selves anymore. The Garou believe in the Triat because it makes sense to their experience and explains the spiritual phenomena they encounter. Mages believe in a number of other things because it fits their experiences. Vampires have various sets of beliefs that aren\u2019t even compatible with each other, which are attempts to rationalize their experiences. <br /> <br /> It\u2019s models within models. Models all the way down. Even if you try to posit a reality underlying all the models, you\u2019re just creating another model (hear that, mages?). WoD has always been thoroughly postmodern like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T00:37:40-07:00","id":1390721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1386339-can-you-make-the-whole-world-of-darkness-work-together-as-one-coherent-universe?p=1390683#post1390683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another thing about Hermetism is that it relies on some nebulous &quot;One&quot;, some monotheistic-unitary force that basically has illusions to the Abrahamic god (which Hermetism seemingly got alot of inspiration from). Thats all fine and dandy, but how does this hold with the existence of the Triat in oWoD? With that standard brought up I don't know how Hermeticism could unify the cosmologies of oWoD since that conflicts right off the bat.</div> </div> </div> </div>It actually does. The Triat, however it formed (umbral existences really are a chicken/egg kinda thing) does not conflict with Hermeticism. Hermeticism allows for any number of gods/demons and worlds between humanity and the one. Changers only look to the Triat/Gaia because it's all that concerns them, some changers even think Gaia is above the Triat which, i think, is ridiculous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T09:03:58-07:00","id":1390792,"title":"","content":"I think that it is a very real possibility - for both the Storyteller and the players - to make the whole WoD work as a coherent setting for an RPG game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T10:43:23-07:00","id":1390809,"title":"","content":"@Muad\u2019Dib thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T13:21:59-07:00","id":1390839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1386339-can-you-make-the-whole-world-of-darkness-work-together-as-one-coherent-universe?p=1390721#post1390721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It actually does. The Triat, however it formed (umbral existences really are a chicken/egg kinda thing) does not conflict with Hermeticism. Hermeticism allows for any number of gods/demons and worlds between humanity and the one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's a major thorny issue with trying to flatten Werewolf into Hermetic philosophy - W:tA absolutely rejects any special importance of humanity. There have been other tool users of that magnitude before, and there will be again; they enjoy no special relationship with a single unitary being or cosmic insight. They just are.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Changers only look to the Triat/Gaia because it's all that concerns them, some changers even think Gaia is above the Triat which, i think, is ridiculous. </div> </div> </div>They look to them because the three are palpable forces that often reach out and touch someone, and it usually ends really badly for the one they touched. They're also major flavors of cosmic existence that other, seemingly unrelated beings can fall into feeling like because actions, especially those writ large or with grand ambition, attract their attention. The more you engage in a set of actions in line with the Triat, the closer you move to them, until you wake up one day and realize that one, you're an alien being with little in common with those around you, and two, you don't see anything wrong with that, but rather with your surroundings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T13:31:39-07:00","id":1390842,"title":"","content":"I think that is a temptation fit try to fit everything else into the Mage world cosmology because, in a very broad sense, it can superficially encompass just about any other cosmology. Superficially, meaning that the appearance of God or the Wyrm or whatever can appear within it, but they lose their cosmological important. Essentially, it's unfair to those other cosmologies (and their gaminess) that are forced into becoming just one among countless other myths that human minds make seem real. That may not matter to some, but I do think that we lose something of value in doing this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T14:21:19-07:00","id":1390850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1386339-can-you-make-the-whole-world-of-darkness-work-together-as-one-coherent-universe?p=1390721#post1390721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It actually does. The Triat, however it formed (umbral existences really are a chicken/egg kinda thing) does not conflict with Hermeticism. Hermeticism allows for any number of gods/demons and worlds between humanity and the one. Changers only look to the Triat/Gaia because it's all that concerns them, some changers even think Gaia is above the Triat which, i think, is ridiculous.</div> </div> </div> </div>But I think the point being made here, referring to Black Flag, Saur Ops, Sergeant, and Shakanaka's previous posts, is that a &quot;Unified World of Darkness&quot; that relies too much on real-world Hermeticism and Gnosticism is going to result in a Mage-centric perspective even if that isn't your explicit intention, because the Mage model was itself heavily influenced by those frameworks. Your own post demonstrates this when you note how Hermeticism accommodates &quot;gods/demons and worlds <i>between</i> humanity and the one.&quot; (Emphasis mine)<br /> <br /> Explicit in this model is a notion of God/the One which is clearly analogous to the Abrahamic concept, with the Triat's role being lesser or subordinate to some extent.<br /> <br /> Less explicit is the point Saur Ops made previously about Hermeticism/Gnosticism being anthropocentric, with humans having a special relationship to divinity that simply doesn't mesh with WtA but <i>does</i> mesh well with Mage.<br /> <br /> Side note: I resolve the confusion of whether Gaia created the Triat or not by having there be two entities referred to as &quot;Gaia&quot;; one the Celestine of Earth, the other being the Higher Power embodied by the Triat.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T17:11:58-07:00","id":1390876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1386339-can-you-make-the-whole-world-of-darkness-work-together-as-one-coherent-universe?p=1390850#post1390850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Side note: I resolve the confusion of whether Gaia created the Triat or not by having there be two entities referred to as &quot;Gaia&quot;; one the Celestine of Earth, the other being the Higher Power embodied by the Triat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, W:tA cosmology is a bit weird in that regard. If Gaia is beyond the Triat, if she represents the universe or reality itself, then there is no way that humans hurting the environment is in any way harmful to her - unless the planet Earth itself is the center of existence and that gets into Mage territory. If Gaia is merely a spirit of earth\u2019s biome, then human activity could indeed threaten her but she would far far beneath the Triat and her destruction wouldn\u2019t be particularly significant to the universe. Werewolf cosmology does seem quite geocentric to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T17:33:47-07:00","id":1390879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1386339-can-you-make-the-whole-world-of-darkness-work-together-as-one-coherent-universe?p=1390876#post1390876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, W:tA cosmology is a bit weird in that regard. If Gaia is beyond the Triat, if she represents the universe or reality itself, then there is no way that humans hurting the environment is in any way harmful to her - unless the planet Earth itself is the center of existence and that gets into Mage territory. If Gaia is merely a spirit of earth\u2019s biome, then human activity could indeed threaten her but she would far far beneath the Triat and her destruction wouldn\u2019t be particularly significant to the universe. Werewolf cosmology does seem quite geocentric to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>And like Mage, that makes sense if you understand their cosmology as being Their Perspective, not Truth <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> That's why I find the best way to be &quot;fair&quot; to all cosmologies is to let them all be correct to some degree, but less informed the further outside their own context they get, Blind People Describing an Elephant. I think you have a better chance of keeping some of the themes of every game intact by being willing to undermine them all to some extent, rather than undermining most of them to an unforgivable degree by placing one particular perspective on a pedestal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T19:25:00-07:00","id":1390892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1386339-can-you-make-the-whole-world-of-darkness-work-together-as-one-coherent-universe?p=1390876#post1390876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, W:tA cosmology is a bit weird in that regard. If Gaia is beyond the Triat, if she represents the universe or reality itself, then there is no way that humans hurting the environment is in any way harmful to her - unless the planet Earth itself is the center of existence and that gets into Mage territory. If Gaia is merely a spirit of earth\u2019s biome, then human activity could indeed threaten her but she would far far beneath the Triat and her destruction wouldn\u2019t be particularly significant to the universe. Werewolf cosmology does seem quite geocentric to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Two things. The first is the possibility of a chain of spiritual ills moving upward through nested avatar hierarchies. The second is that if there are many Gaias, as the Wagnerieans posit in W:tA, there's no guarantee that they aren't embroiled in their own struggles, possibly even having lost already. As such, what goes on in this cosmic neighborhood becomes very important, because it can't lean on anything else for a feeling of safety. There is no place across the stars to flee, there is no wandering spirit that can pull your fat from the frying pan - it all comes down to the here and now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}